Subject: Fix: lift the flying shells' ground shadow (issue #18)
Upstream-base: 7a6bf165d9f1c5914181c079c7d4bfa7204f3509

A fix of the original game's presentation, always on and without a switch
(owner decision, 2026-10-12). It lives in the tweak series so the faithful
series stays retail.

Thrown shells (KoopaShellObject: green, spiny and the other trail shells)
draw a round ground shadow, a "global/ball_shadow" quad on the unshadowed
layer with depth test and no depth write, placed 1/64 above the stadium's
shadow height. On some Windows PCs that shadow flickered while the shell
moved (issue #18), which looks like depth fighting with the field; Linux
does not show it. The original keeps character shadows at the stadium's
co-planar height (0.1 above the field).

The shell shadow now sits 0.1 higher. Size, fade, alpha, texture and draw
order are unchanged; from the game cameras the lift is not visible.

diff --git a/src/Game/Drawable/DrawableKoopaShell.cpp b/src/Game/Drawable/DrawableKoopaShell.cpp
index 5d7ee2f..9244835 100644
--- a/src/Game/Drawable/DrawableKoopaShell.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Drawable/DrawableKoopaShell.cpp
@@ -78,6 +78,12 @@ static void DrawShadow(const nlMatrix4& matrix, float scale)
     }
 
     groundHeight = 0.015625f + groundHeight;
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // Port fix, always on (issue #18): lift the shell's ground shadow 0.1 more.
+    // At 1/64 above the field it flickered on some Windows PCs; the original
+    // keeps character shadows at the co-planar height (0.1) instead.
+    groundHeight += 0.1f;
+#endif
     nlVec3Set(position, matrix.m41, matrix.m42, groundHeight);
     extent.x = size;
     extent.y = size;
